--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- chain in a MoorDyn-C current grid in x, y, z and time (Currents 5), 120 s
-- The 410 m studless chain of dynamic_chain_waves.dat with its anchor 390 m from the held
-- fairlead in 50 m of water: about 90 m hangs free and the rest lies on the seabed, held by
-- seabed friction (0.7). The current varies along the line, in depth and in time, read from
-- current_profile_4d.txt in this folder (generate_kinematics.py writes it). Line 1 of the file
-- gives the grid size nx ny nz nt, lines 2-5 the x, y, z and t coordinates, line 6 is a header,
-- and each later row is one grid point `x y z t ux uy uz`. Here the current runs across the line
-- (+Y), grows from 0.4 m/s at the fairlead (x = 0) to 1.2 m/s at x = 400 m, is sheared to 30 %
-- of that at the seabed, and ramps in linearly over the first 30 s from still water, the static
-- start. CableDyn interpolates the grid at every node and time as MoorDyn-C v2.7.1 does: linear
-- between grid coordinates, held beyond the end ones, with no fluid acceleration. The hanging
-- chain is pushed out of its plane (L1N5py, the node 40 m from the fairlead); friction holds
-- the grounded chain.
